{{!-- One author's face, in the author's own context: {{#primary_author}}{{> "post/avatar"}}{{/primary_author}}.

	size / textSize    the two sizes the design draws it at (34px in a byline, 56px in the bio card)

The design has one drawing here — a tinted badge holding the writer's initials — and Ghost has
two cases. A publication whose writers uploaded a photo has a photo, and dropping it to draw a
monogram instead would be a theme overruling its own data, so the photo wins when it exists and
the badge is the fallback.

The badge carries ONE letter where the design draws two. Handlebars cannot take a substring and
Ghost ships no helper that can, so a second initial would have to come from a lookup the template
does not have; `{{name.[0]}}` is index access on the name string, which is the whole of what is
available. Recorded as a concession in DECISIONS.md.

NEITHER `loading="lazy"` NOR `decoding="async"`, which the design source puts only on images below
the fold. This one sits under the title, it is a 3KB thumbnail, and both places it appears on a
post request the same URL — so deferring the second saves nothing the first has not already done.
It is also what made the identity harness lie: two captures of the same page differed by exactly
these two 34px and 56px squares, because both attributes tell the browser it may paint a frame
without this image, and a headless screenshot takes that permission. --}}
{{#if profile_image}}
	<img
		src="{{img_url profile_image size="xs"}}"
		alt=""
		class="{{size}} flex-none rounded-full object-cover">
{{else}}
	<span
		aria-hidden="true"
		class="{{size}} {{textSize}} bg-accent-soft font-ui text-accent-strong grid flex-none place-items-center rounded-full font-semibold">{{name.[0]}}</span>
{{/if}}
